{"conversation_id":"550e4a17-810a-4183-b0c2-593a555f3528","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\"agent\":\"Frontend Engineer\",\"areas_affected\":[\"app/status/page.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusCard.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusBadge.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusRefreshButton.tsx\",\"components/layout/Footer.tsx\",\"types/index.ts\",\"tests/status.test.tsx\",\"docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md\",\"docs/engineering/STATUS_PAGE.md\",\"app/api/status/route.ts\"],\"contracts\":[\"API Contract GET /api/status: Returns HTTP 200 (or HTTP 503 on service outage) with application/json body: { status: 'operational' | 'degraded' | 'down', version: string, environment: 'production' | 'preview' | 'development', timestamp: string, services: { api: { status: 'operational' | 'down', latency_ms?: number }, database: { status: 'connected' | 'disconnected' | 'mock', latency_ms?: number } } }.\",\"Caching Contract: Endpoint GET /api/status must include 'Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, proxy-revalidate' and frontend fetch must specify { cache: 'no-store' } to avoid stale status indicators.\",\"TypeScript Contract: types/index.ts exports SystemStatusResponse, ServiceStatus ('operational' | 'degraded' | 'down'), and StatusEnvironment ('production' | 'preview' | 'development').\",\"Route Access Contract: The /status page and /api/status endpoint must be explicitly public in lib/supabase/proxy.ts, accessible without authentication.\"],\"proposed_tasks\":[{\"depends_on\":[],\"description\":\"Define TypeScript interfaces in types/index.ts for the status API contract (SystemStatusResponse, ServiceHealth, StatusEnvironment) and UI state.\",\"id\":\"task-01-api-contract-types\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-01-api-contract-types\"],\"description\":\"Implement backend GET /api/status route in app/api/status/route.ts returning availability, version, environment, and DB health check with proper cache control (no-store).\",\"id\":\"task-02-backend-status-endpoint\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Backend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-01-api-contract-types\"],\"description\":\"Develop status presentation components (StatusCard, StatusBadge, ServiceHealthList, StatusRefreshButton) using Tailwind v4, Lucide icons, and ARIA live regions for accessibility.\",\"id\":\"task-03-status-ui-components\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-02-backend-status-endpoint\",\"task-03-status-ui-components\"],\"description\":\"Implement public Next.js page at app/status/page.tsx integrating client-side fetching/polling, loading skeletons, error fallback handling, and metadata.\",\"id\":\"task-04-status-page-route\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-04-status-page-route\"],\"description\":\"Update components/layout/Footer.tsx to include an accessible link to /status without affecting existing navigation flows.\",\"id\":\"task-05-footer-navigation\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-04-status-page-route\"],\"description\":\"Write comprehensive Vitest and React Testing Library tests in tests/status.test.tsx covering loading skeletons, operational status, degraded/down states, error handling, and manual refresh.\",\"id\":\"task-06-frontend-tests\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-05-footer-navigation\",\"task-06-frontend-tests\"],\"description\":\"Create docs/engineering/STATUS_PAGE.md, register it in docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md, and run verification via npm run verify.\",\"id\":\"task-07-documentation-verification\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"}],\"questions_or_unknowns\":[\"What is the canonical source for the backend version string (e.g., package.json version, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, or custom release environment variable)?\",\"Should the status page implement automatic periodic polling (e.g., every 30 or 60 seconds) in addition to manual refresh, and should it pause when the browser tab is in the background?\",\"Should the status page be completely public (linked in the public footer) or restricted to authenticated administrators?\",\"Are external dependencies beyond Supabase (such as email service or external CDN) required to be tracked in the status breakdown?\"],\"risks\":[\"Information disclosure: Leaking internal configuration details, environment secrets, full error traces, or sensitive server infrastructure metadata through the status endpoint or UI.\",\"Stale status due to CDN/browser caching: Next.js or edge intermediate caches caching GET /api/status responses, presenting outdated healthy status during an active outage.\",\"Cascading service disruption / self-DoS: High-frequency polling on /status triggering intensive database health checks, exacerbating database load during high traffic or partial outages.\",\"False negative status on client network interruptions: Transient client-side connectivity drops misrepresenting backend availability as a platform outage rather than local network failure.\",\"Route guard obstruction: Regression in proxy.ts redirecting unauthenticated users visiting /status to /login.\"],\"summary\":\"Design and implement a user-facing health and status page (/status) in Next.js 16 (App Router) and React 19 displaying real-time API availability, backend version, application environment, and database connectivity. The implementation encompasses responsive UI components styled with Tailwind CSS v4, accessible status badges, resilient client-side polling with error and loading states, manual refresh functionality, navigation integration via the site footer, and thorough Vitest unit/component tests—conditioned upon the backend delivering the GET /api/status endpoint contract.\",\"tests\":[\"Unit/Component test: Renders operational status badge, backend version string, and current application environment when API returns HTTP 200 healthy response.\",\"Unit/Component test: Renders loading skeleton while status data is being fetched.\",\"Unit/Component test: Renders degraded or down error banner when GET /api/status returns 503 or fails with network error.\",\"Unit/Component test: Clicking the manual refresh button triggers re-fetch, shows loading state, and updates the last checked timestamp.\",\"Accessibility test: Status indicators provide proper ARIA attributes (role='status', aria-live='polite') for assistive technology.\",\"Gate verification: Full test suite, linting, typechecking, and documentation checks pass via npm run verify.\"],\"toolAction\":\"Submitting status page planning result\",\"toolSummary\":\"Planning submission\"}\n","duration_seconds":155.1265154,"num_turns":1,"structured_output":{"agent":"Frontend Engineer","areas_affected":["app/status/page.tsx","components/status/StatusCard.tsx","components/status/StatusBadge.tsx","components/status/StatusRefreshButton.tsx","components/layout/Footer.tsx","types/index.ts","tests/status.test.tsx","docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md","docs/engineering/STATUS_PAGE.md","app/api/status/route.ts"],"contracts":["API Contract GET /api/status: Returns HTTP 200 (or HTTP 503 on service outage) with application/json body: { status: 'operational' | 'degraded' | 'down', version: string, environment: 'production' | 'preview' | 'development', timestamp: string, services: { api: { status: 'operational' | 'down', latency_ms?: number }, database: { status: 'connected' | 'disconnected' | 'mock', latency_ms?: number } } }.","Caching Contract: Endpoint GET /api/status must include 'Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, proxy-revalidate' and frontend fetch must specify { cache: 'no-store' } to avoid stale status indicators.","TypeScript Contract: types/index.ts exports SystemStatusResponse, ServiceStatus ('operational' | 'degraded' | 'down'), and StatusEnvironment ('production' | 'preview' | 'development').","Route Access Contract: The /status page and /api/status endpoint must be explicitly public in lib/supabase/proxy.ts, accessible without authentication."],"proposed_tasks":[{"depends_on":[],"description":"Define TypeScript interfaces in types/index.ts for the status API contract (SystemStatusResponse, ServiceHealth, StatusEnvironment) and UI state.","id":"task-01-api-contract-types","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-01-api-contract-types"],"description":"Implement backend GET /api/status route in app/api/status/route.ts returning availability, version, environment, and DB health check with proper cache control (no-store).","id":"task-02-backend-status-endpoint","suggested_owner":"Backend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-01-api-contract-types"],"description":"Develop status presentation components (StatusCard, StatusBadge, ServiceHealthList, StatusRefreshButton) using Tailwind v4, Lucide icons, and ARIA live regions for accessibility.","id":"task-03-status-ui-components","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-02-backend-status-endpoint","task-03-status-ui-components"],"description":"Implement public Next.js page at app/status/page.tsx integrating client-side fetching/polling, loading skeletons, error fallback handling, and metadata.","id":"task-04-status-page-route","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-04-status-page-route"],"description":"Update components/layout/Footer.tsx to include an accessible link to /status without affecting existing navigation flows.","id":"task-05-footer-navigation","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-04-status-page-route"],"description":"Write comprehensive Vitest and React Testing Library tests in tests/status.test.tsx covering loading skeletons, operational status, degraded/down states, error handling, and manual refresh.","id":"task-06-frontend-tests","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"},{"depends_on":["task-05-footer-navigation","task-06-frontend-tests"],"description":"Create docs/engineering/STATUS_PAGE.md, register it in docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md, and run verification via npm run verify.","id":"task-07-documentation-verification","suggested_owner":"Frontend Engineer"}],"questions_or_unknowns":["What is the canonical source for the backend version string (e.g., package.json version, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, or custom release environment variable)?","Should the status page implement automatic periodic polling (e.g., every 30 or 60 seconds) in addition to manual refresh, and should it pause when the browser tab is in the background?","Should the status page be completely public (linked in the public footer) or restricted to authenticated administrators?","Are external dependencies beyond Supabase (such as email service or external CDN) required to be tracked in the status breakdown?"],"risks":["Information disclosure: Leaking internal configuration details, environment secrets, full error traces, or sensitive server infrastructure metadata through the status endpoint or UI.","Stale status due to CDN/browser caching: Next.js or edge intermediate caches caching GET /api/status responses, presenting outdated healthy status during an active outage.","Cascading service disruption / self-DoS: High-frequency polling on /status triggering intensive database health checks, exacerbating database load during high traffic or partial outages.","False negative status on client network interruptions: Transient client-side connectivity drops misrepresenting backend availability as a platform outage rather than local network failure.","Route guard obstruction: Regression in proxy.ts redirecting unauthenticated users visiting /status to /login."],"summary":"Design and implement a user-facing health and status page (/status) in Next.js 16 (App Router) and React 19 displaying real-time API availability, backend version, application environment, and database connectivity. The implementation encompasses responsive UI components styled with Tailwind CSS v4, accessible status badges, resilient client-side polling with error and loading states, manual refresh functionality, navigation integration via the site footer, and thorough Vitest unit/component tests—conditioned upon the backend delivering the GET /api/status endpoint contract.","tests":["Unit/Component test: Renders operational status badge, backend version string, and current application environment when API returns HTTP 200 healthy response.","Unit/Component test: Renders loading skeleton while status data is being fetched.","Unit/Component test: Renders degraded or down error banner when GET /api/status returns 503 or fails with network error.","Unit/Component test: Clicking the manual refresh button triggers re-fetch, shows loading state, and updates the last checked timestamp.","Accessibility test: Status indicators provide proper ARIA attributes (role='status', aria-live='polite') for assistive technology.","Gate verification: Full test suite, linting, typechecking, and documentation checks pass via npm run verify."]},"json_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["agent","summary","areas_affected","proposed_tasks","contracts","risks","tests","questions_or_unknowns"],"properties":{"agent":{"type":"string"},"summary":{"type":"string"},"areas_affected":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"proposed_tasks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["id","description","suggested_owner","depends_on"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string"},"suggested_owner":{"type":"string"},"depends_on":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},"contracts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"risks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"tests":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"questions_or_unknowns":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}},"usage":{"input_tokens":220020,"output_tokens":19734,"thinking_tokens":16106,"cache_read_tokens":1306813,"total_tokens":239754}}
